# diagram-dsl Development Rules

## Backwards Compatibility

**No backwards compatibility is required for this library.**

This library is still work in progress and does not have any users yet. Breaking changes are acceptable and encouraged if they improve the API or implementation.

When making changes:
- Do not maintain old APIs for compatibility
- Do not add migration guides
- Do not worry about breaking changes
- Focus on making the best possible API and implementation
- Update documentation to reflect current state only

## Arrow Rendering

Arrows must connect boxes at their attachment points:
- Attachment points are the centers of the four rectangle sides (top, bottom, left, right)
- Arrows should go from one attachment point to another attachment point
- Calculate which attachment points to use based on the relative positions of the boxes

## Arrow Labels

Arrow labels must be legible:
- Either position them to not intersect with the arrow line
- Or use a semi-transparent background to ensure readability when they overlap
- Labels should be centered along the arrow path
